Design:
```
#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
pub struct RingBuf<T: Copy, const N: usize> {
    data: [core::mem::MaybeUninit<T>; N],
    head: usize, // index of next write? or oldest?
    len: usize,
}
```
Need new, push, pop, len.

Semantics: push adds to back, pop removes from front. Ring buffer with head = index of oldest element, tail = index of next write. len = number elements.

Implementation:
```
impl<T: Copy, const N: usize> RingBuf<T, N> {
    pub const fn new() -> Self {
        Self { data: [core::mem::MaybeUninit::uninit(); N], head: 0, len: 0 }
    }
    pub fn push(&mut self, value: T) -> Option<T> { // maybe returns Option<T> if full? 
        if self.len == N { return None; }
        let idx = (self.head + self.len) % N;
        self.data[idx].write(value);
        self.len += 1;
        Some(value)
    }
    pub fn pop(&mut self) -> Option<T> {
        if self.len == 0 { return None; }
        let idx = self.head;
        let value = unsafe { self.data[idx].assume_init() };
        self.head = (self.head + 1) % N;
        self.len -= 1;
        Some(value)
    }
    pub fn len(&self) -> usize { self.len }
}
```
